SYSMON VERSION 0.94 CHANGELOG
================================

This release represents a major update with critical bug fixes, new wishlist features,
and comprehensive web-UI enhancements.

MAJOR IMPROVEMENTS
==================

Wishlist Features Implemented
------------------------------
* config minnumfailures <n>
  - Sets minimum consecutive failures before host appears in status file
  - Reduces false alarms from transient network issues
  - Default is 1 (show after first failure)

* config flaptime <minutes>
  - Keeps host displaying as green for N minutes after recovery
  - Prevents "flapping" appearance when hosts go up/down repeatedly
  - Default is 0 (disabled)
  - Uses new last_recovery timestamp field in hostinfo struct

* Per-object pageinterval
  - Allows different hosts to have different re-page intervals
  - Critical hosts can be paged more frequently
  - config pageinterval <minutes>; inside object{} blocks
  - Falls back to global pageinterval when not set
  - Note: Requires flex to regenerate parser.c for changes to take effect

Web-UI Enhancements (v0.94)
----------------------------
* Fixed Critical 403 Errors
  - Changed from STAT to STATO command (eliminates hostname vs unique_name mismatch)
  - Fixed GetObjectsXML() to also use STATO instead of STAT
  - Dramatically improves performance (no wasted SHOWOBJ calls)

* Session Logger
  - Captures all protocol operations with errors
  - Maintains circular buffers: last 500 entries, last 100 errors
  - API endpoints: /api/admin/session-log, /api/admin/session-errors
  - Replaced all stderr logging with structured logging

* Admin Page Session Log Display
  - Shows last 5 errors with timestamps, commands, responses
  - Shows last 50 protocol operations
  - Auto-refreshes every 5 seconds
  - Color-coded: blue for success, red for errors

* Dashboard Improvements
  - Added daemon version and uptime display
  - Fixed layout shifting bugs
  - Removed unnecessary UI elements (PID, Config File, check types chart)
  - Added hover tooltips to stats showing host lists by category

* Dual-View Host Display
  - Comparison View: Ultra-compact grid showing up to 30+ hosts
  - Table View: Comprehensive sortable table with detailed stats
  - Toggle button to switch between views
  - Both views prominently display hostnames
  - Hover tooltips with full host details

* Compact UI
  - Increased grid density (4-5 columns on large screens)
  - Reduced padding and font sizes throughout
  - Can now display 15-25 hosts per screen vs 6-9 before
  - Optimized for quick scanning of entire infrastructure

* Documentation
  - Added statustempdir to sysmon.conf.man
  - Removed all JSON mode references (never implemented)
  - Updated README with correct XML mode documentation
  - All markdown files converted to plain ASCII text

Daemon Improvements
-------------------
* Fixed ICMP race condition causing false negative ping detections
* Increased ping timeout to 2 seconds for reliability
* Fixed NULL pointer dereferences in dump_to_file()
* Reliable XML transmission with error checking
* Added statustempdir for privilege-dropped operation
* Proper handling of all response codes (333, 403, 444)
* Fixed ReadString() EOF handling bugs

TECHNICAL DETAILS
=================

Parser Changes (requires flex to take effect)
----------------------------------------------
* Added parser_i_minnumfailures and parser_minnumfailures variables
* Added parser_i_flaptime and parser_flaptime variables
* Added parser_i_pageinterval and parser_obj_i_pageinterval variables
* Updated object creation to use per-object overrides when set
* Added validation for negative values and error handling

Struct Changes
--------------
* Added last_recovery field to hostinfo struct (for flaptime)
* Added pageinterval field to hostinfo struct (for per-object intervals)
* Proper initialization of all new fields

API Endpoints Added
-------------------
* GET /api/admin/session-log?limit=N
* GET /api/admin/session-errors?limit=N

KNOWN ISSUES
============

* pageinterval feature requires flex to regenerate parser.c
  - parser.l has been updated with the code
  - Install flex and run 'make clean && make' to enable
  - Without flex, only pre-existing features will work

UPGRADE NOTES
=============

1. The web-UI now shows version 0.94 correctly
2. All JSON mode references have been removed (never implemented)
3. Parser changes require flex for regeneration
4. Session logging replaces stderr output for protocol debugging

